IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fwa-employee`
IMPORT `fwa-day-one`

-- Fair Work Act 2009 (with the Fair Work Regulations 2009), day one -- the employee's questions, worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by
-- hand from the deposited text (the section or regulation is named beside each), never copied from the encoding's
-- output. Facts are from the Western Australian lives (workbench scenarios/au/wa/cradle-to-grave-*), named by event id.
-- Facts the life does not state are marked HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- c040 (2024-02-05): Chloe starts the graduate program at Ironbark Logistics Pty Ltd, a large national system employer,
-- full-time and ongoing, $70,000 a year, with a probation clause; no award stated. "What must a contract contain; what
-- are the minimum standards; can probation do what it says?"
-- d044 (2031-06-01): Daniel's Jarrah Legal Technologies Pty Ltd takes on its first three employees (a small business
-- employer, s 23). The life does not say whether any is casual or on a fixed term: those cases are HYPOTHETICAL.

-- Chloe dismissed in her first month, on probation (c040; the dismissal is HYPOTHETICAL).
`Chloe dismissed in her first month on probation (c040)` MEANS MyTermination WITH
    `how it ended` IS `my employer ended it`
    `I was casual` IS FALSE
    `I was employed for a specified period, task or season` IS FALSE
    `it was for serious misconduct` IS FALSE
    `years of continuous service` IS 0.08
    `my age` IS 20
    `my job is no longer needed by anyone` IS FALSE
    `it was ordinary and customary turnover of labour` IS FALSE
    `my employer is insolvent or bankrupt` IS FALSE
    `employees counted under s 23` IS 200
    `I am an apprentice` IS FALSE
    `an industry-specific redundancy scheme in my award applies` IS FALSE

§ `ss 44, 60, 61 -- the NES as a floor`

-- c040, "what are the minimum standards": s 61(2) lists twelve matters, (a), (b), (ba), (c) to (h), (ha), (i), (j).
#ASSERT count `What are the National Employment Standards` EQUALS 12
#ASSERT `What are the National Employment Standards` EQUALS LIST `maximum weekly hours (Division 3)`, `requests for flexible working arrangements (Division 4)`, `casual employment (Division 4A)`, `parental leave and related entitlements (Division 5)`, `annual leave (Division 6)`, `personal/carer's leave, compassionate leave and paid family and domestic violence leave (Division 7)`, `community service leave (Division 8)`, `long service leave (Division 9)`, `public holidays (Division 10)`, `superannuation contributions (Division 10A)`, `notice of termination and redundancy pay (Division 11)`, `the Fair Work Information Statement and the Casual Employment Information Statement (Division 12)`

-- c040, "can probation do what it says?": a probation clause that gives Chloe less than the NES (say, no notice while
-- on probation) cannot displace them (s 61(1)); acting on it would contravene s 44.
#ASSERT `Can my contract give me less than the NES` TRUE `it gives less than the NES on an NES matter` EQUALS `the NES apply in full: the term cannot displace them (s 61(1)), and acting on it would contravene s 44`
-- A term giving more (say five weeks' annual leave against the four of s 87) operates.
#ASSERT `Can my contract give me less than the NES` TRUE `it gives the same as the NES, or more` EQUALS `the term can operate: it does not undercut the NES`
-- An agreement the NES itself allows (say s 64 averaging, agreed in writing) operates.
#ASSERT `Can my contract give me less than the NES` TRUE `it is an agreement that an NES provision itself allows` EQUALS `the term can operate: it does not undercut the NES`
-- s 60: an unpaid vocational placement (c032's question) is not national system employment: not covered.
#ASSERT `Can my contract give me less than the NES` FALSE `it gives less than the NES on an NES matter` EQUALS `not covered: the NES apply only to a national system employee (s 60)`

-- c040: the NES have no probation exception. Dismissed in her first month, Chloe still gets 1 week's notice: s 117(3)
-- "Not more than 1 year: 1 week"; she is 20, so no extra week; s 123 excludes no employee on probation.
#ASSERT `How many weeks of notice must I get` `Chloe dismissed in her first month on probation (c040)` EQUALS 1

-- s 44: failing to give an NES entitlement to a national system employee contravenes it; no duty to a non-employee.
#ASSERT `Has my employer contravened the NES` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Has my employer contravened the NES` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Has my employer contravened the NES` TRUE FALSE

§ `s 125 -- the Fair Work Information Statement`

-- c040: Chloe, new to Ironbark, must be given the statement before or as soon as practicable after 5 February 2024.
#ASSERT `Must my employer give me the Fair Work Information Statement` TRUE FALSE
-- s 125(2): re-employed by the same employer within 12 months of the last statement: not again.
#ASSERT NOT `Must my employer give me the Fair Work Information Statement` TRUE TRUE
-- s 60: not a national system employee: no duty under this Act.
#ASSERT NOT `Must my employer give me the Fair Work Information Statement` FALSE FALSE

-- ss 44, 61(2)(j): not given, and as soon as practicable has passed -- a contravention of the NES itself.
#ASSERT `Has my employer contravened the NES over the Fair Work Information Statement` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE
-- Given: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT `Has my employer contravened the NES over the Fair Work Information Statement` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
-- Not given yet, but it is still not later than "as soon as practicable": no contravention yet.
#ASSERT NOT `Has my employer contravened the NES over the Fair Work Information Statement` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE

§ `ss 125, 125B(1)(a), 333K -- the statements on day one`

-- c040: Chloe, full-time and ongoing: the Fair Work Information Statement only.
#ASSERT `Which statements must I be given when I start` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `these statements` (LIST `the Fair Work Information Statement (s 125)`)
-- d044 (HYPOTHETICAL that the employee is casual): the Fair Work and the Casual Employment Information Statements.
#ASSERT `Which statements must I be given when I start` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `these statements` (LIST `the Fair Work Information Statement (s 125)`, `the Casual Employment Information Statement (s 125B(1)(a))`)
-- d044 (HYPOTHETICAL: a 12-month contract): the Fair Work and the Fixed Term Contract Information Statements.
#ASSERT `Which statements must I be given when I start` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `these statements` (LIST `the Fair Work Information Statement (s 125)`, `the Fixed Term Contract Information Statement (s 333K)`)
-- A casual re-employed within 12 months of both statements (ss 125(2), 125B(3)): none again.
#ASSERT `Which statements must I be given when I start` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `these statements` EMPTY
-- Not a national system employee: not covered.
#ASSERT `Which statements must I be given when I start` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered: these duties are owed only to a national system employee`

§ `s 125B -- the Casual Employment Information Statement`

-- d044 (HYPOTHETICAL casual at Jarrah, 3 employees, a small business employer under s 23(1)):
-- (1)(a) at the start: yes.
#ASSERT `Must my employer give me the Casual Employment Information Statement` TRUE TRUE `starting as a casual` 4 FALSE
-- (1)(b) at 6 months: no, s 125B(2) -- Jarrah is still a small business employer.
#ASSERT NOT `Must my employer give me the Casual Employment Information Statement` TRUE TRUE `6 months after starting` 4 FALSE
-- (1)(c)(i) at 12 months: yes; s 125B(2) does not reach (c)(i).
#ASSERT `Must my employer give me the Casual Employment Information Statement` TRUE TRUE `12 months after starting` 4 FALSE
-- (1)(c)(ii) at the end of each further 12 months: no while Jarrah is small.
#ASSERT NOT `Must my employer give me the Casual Employment Information Statement` TRUE TRUE `the end of each further 12 months` 4 FALSE
-- Had Jarrah grown to 15 by then (s 23(1): "fewer than 15"), the 6-month and later statements are owed.
#ASSERT `Must my employer give me the Casual Employment Information Statement` TRUE TRUE `6 months after starting` 15 FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Must my employer give me the Casual Employment Information Statement` TRUE TRUE `6 months after starting` 14 FALSE
#ASSERT `Must my employer give me the Casual Employment Information Statement` TRUE TRUE `the end of each further 12 months` 15 FALSE
-- c040: Chloe is not a casual: never.
#ASSERT NOT `Must my employer give me the Casual Employment Information Statement` FALSE TRUE `starting as a casual` 200 FALSE

§ `s 333K -- the Fixed Term Contract Information Statement`

#ASSERT `Must my employer give me the Fixed Term Contract Information Statement` TRUE TRUE
-- c040: Chloe's graduate job is ongoing.
#ASSERT NOT `Must my employer give me the Fixed Term Contract Information Statement` TRUE FALSE

§ `s 535, regs 3.31-3.42 -- records`

-- c040: Chloe, salaried, no bonus or overtime loading stated, entitled to leave, super payable (c041: 11%): the reg
-- 3.32 basics, reg 3.33(1) pay, reg 3.36(1) leave, reg 3.37 super.
#ASSERT `What records must my employer keep about me` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS LIST `names, full-time or part-time, permanent, temporary or casual, start date, and the employer's ABN if any (reg 3.32)`, `the rate of pay, gross and net amounts paid, and deductions (reg 3.33(1))`, `leave taken and the leave balance (reg 3.36(1))`, `superannuation contributions: amounts, period, dates, fund, and why they were owed, including the fund choice and its date (reg 3.37)`
-- d044 (HYPOTHETICAL casual, paid by the hour with a casual loading; super at 12%): also hours (reg 3.33(2)) and the
-- loading (reg 3.33(3)). Casuals are entitled to some leave (unpaid carer's and compassionate leave, paid family and
-- domestic violence leave), so reg 3.36(1) applies.
#ASSERT count (`What records must my employer keep about me` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS 6
-- When the employment ends (reg 3.40), how it ended and who ended it are added (Chloe's facts, HYPOTHETICAL ending).
#ASSERT elem `how the employment ended and who ended it (reg 3.40)` (`What records must my employer keep about me` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- Every condition at once: all twelve kinds.
#ASSERT count (`What records must my employer keep about me` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS 12

-- s 535(1): 7 years.
#ASSERT `How many years must my employer keep my records` EQUALS 7

-- Reg 3.42(3): kept where she works: within 3 business days there, or posted within 14 days. (4): otherwise as soon as
-- practicable.
#ASSERT `How quickly must I be shown my records` TRUE EQUALS `within 3 business days at the workplace, or posted within 14 days (reg 3.42(3))`
#ASSERT `How quickly must I be shown my records` FALSE EQUALS `as soon as practicable, at the workplace or by post (reg 3.42(4))`

§ `s 557C -- no records`

-- An underpayment claim under the NES (s 44) where no leave record was kept: the employer must disprove it.
#ASSERT `Must my employer disprove what I allege` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE
-- Unless the court accepts the employer's reasonable excuse (s 557C(2)).
#ASSERT NOT `Must my employer disprove what I allege` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE
-- The records were kept: the ordinary burden.
#ASSERT NOT `Must my employer disprove what I allege` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE
